## 1. Store — `backend/src/tyche/market_data/deep_dive_store.py`

`DEEP_DIVE_REL = "signals/stocks/deep_dive"` — a per-ticker Parquet directory (one file per ticker: `signals/stocks/deep_dive/{TICKER}.parquet`).

`DeepDiveStore`:

- `write_batch(payloads: dict[str, TickerDeepDiveResponse], ctx=None) -> int` — one Parquet per ticker, single row, columns: `ticker`, `as_of_date`, `computed_at` (UTC ISO), `payload_json` (str = `response.model_dump_json()`). Storing the serialized payload avoids fragile nested-array Parquet schemas and is schema-evolution safe.
- `read_ticker(ticker, ctx=None) -> tuple[TickerDeepDiveResponse, str] | None` — returns `(payload, as_of_date)` via `TickerDeepDiveResponse.model_validate_json(...)`, or `None` if missing.
- `write_ticker(ticker, payload, ctx=None)` — single-ticker write (used by route write-back).

Use `StoreBackend` / `context_for_data_access()` so it works local + GCS (copy `stocks_deep_dips_store.py`).

